-- title:
--   A balanced single-coordinate raise supplies a balanced uniformly shifted source lift
-- statement:
--   A balanced single-coordinate raise supplies a balanced uniformly shifted source lift.
--
--   Let $n>0$ and write $I_n=\mathbb Z/n\mathbb Z$, represented by $0,\ldots,n-1$. The symbol $\operatorname{rep}$ takes a residue to its nonnegative representative and leaves ordinary integers unchanged. Residue sums and differences are cyclic; inequalities use representatives. $\mathfrak S(I_n)$ is the permutation group. Function symbols are written in curried notation; a subscript $\#$ means finite cardinality. $\mathrm{Lift}(p,c,d)$ means $\sum_i d(i)=0$ and $i+d(i)\equiv p^{-1}(i)+c\pmod n$ for every residue $i$. $\mathrm{RA}(e,a)(i)=e(i)+n\mathbf1_{i=a}$ raises one coordinate by a period.
--
--   The precise quantified assertion, with all its hypotheses, is
--
--   $$
--   \forall  (n : \mathbb N_{>0}) (p : \mathfrak S(I_n)) (c : I_{n}) (e : I_{n} \to  \mathbb Z) (a : I_{n}), \operatorname{Lift} p (\operatorname{rep}\,c) (\operatorname{RA} e a) \to  \operatorname{Lift} p (\operatorname{rep}\,c + 1) \lambda i \mapsto e i + 1
--   $$
--
--   This identity can be used while tracking the exact cost or structure of the sorting construction.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/snow-ghost/glushkov-lx-lean/blob/8cddcd222b591673dc63475d9d45b9ed5c6eb92c/LX/OddRaisedInversions.lean#L28-L46

